#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059419 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "831f9aa0-099e-5e0c-8a9d-c4828b629f64" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying Expressions in Radians Using the Sum and Difference Formulas"}] :question/id #uuid "1d8679d3-8922-5471-811f-60c8c41c853a" :question/math-academy-id "e-3522" :question/problem "Express $\\cos\\left(x - \\dfrac{\\pi}{2} \\right)$ in terms of $\\sin x$ and $\\cos x$." :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the difference formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cos(u - v) = \\cos u \\cos v + \\sin u \\sin v\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for cosine with $u = x$ and\n\n$$\nv = \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos (x - \\frac{π}{2}) &= \\cos x\\cos (\\frac{π}{2}) + \\sin x\\sin (\\frac{π}{2}) \\\\\n&= \\cos x \\cdot 0 + \\sin x \\cdot 1 \\\\\n&= \\sin x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059420 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "283415d8-47d7-5d42-8836-0c0b0c4efc85" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Exact Values Using the Sum and Difference Formulas"}] :question/id #uuid "bdb79801-7c8f-5b39-8730-85dcc3d9cdd0" :question/math-academy-id "e-3523" :question/problem "Find the exact value of $\\cos \\left(-\\dfrac{\\pi}{12} \\right)$.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $-\\dfrac{\\pi}{12} = \\dfrac{\\pi}{6} - \\dfrac{\\pi}{4}$.*" :question/worked-solution "Recall the difference formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cos(x - y) = \\cos{x}\\cos{y} + \\sin{x}\\sin{y}\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for cosine with\n\n$$\nx = \\dfrac{\\pi}{6}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\ny = \\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos (-\\frac{π}{12}) &= \\cos (\\frac{π}{6} - \\frac{π}{4}) \\\\\n&= \\cos (\\frac{π}{6})\\cos (\\frac{π}{4}) + \\sin (\\frac{π}{6})\\sin (\\frac{π}{4}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} + \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4} + \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{2}}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059552 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c6a58962-cb06-519a-8c64-0dfa3b9c14d7" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying Expressions in Degrees Using the Sum and Difference Formulas"}] :question/id #uuid "b643e820-52c3-5c08-a099-aecbed7b2b2a" :question/math-academy-id "e-9991" :question/problem "Express $\\cos(x - 60^\\circ)$ in terms of $\\sin x$ and $\\cos x$." :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the difference formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cos(u - v) = \\cos{u}\\cos{v} + \\sin{u}\\sin{v}\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for cosine with $u = x$ and\n\n$$\nv = 60^\\circ\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos (x - 60^{∘}) &= \\cos x\\cos 60^{∘} + \\sin x\\sin 60^{∘} \\\\\n&= \\cos x \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} + \\sin x \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\cos x}{2} + \\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\sin x}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\cos x + \\sqrt{3}\\sin x}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256342 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "283415d8-47d7-5d42-8836-0c0b0c4efc85" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Exact Values Using the Sum and Difference Formulas"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e9b4c7e-2c5a-5970-bc30-fba6be72da6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{6}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256344} {:answer/id #uuid "f5a50aa1-263e-5cb1-aeea-9c6a0ad51b82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{6}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256345} {:answer/id #uuid "3df53452-210c-5aa3-bc09-733aabec648d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{6}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256346} {:answer/id #uuid "2a0b6e72-b3b1-5ba7-a8b3-5358a0fb52f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{6}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256347} {:answer/id #uuid "d9c2dc06-5cdb-51b6-b96f-4e13af65fa1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{6}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256348}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3df53452-210c-5aa3-bc09-733aabec648d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{6}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256346} :answer-field/id #uuid "3661e593-362f-552c-80aa-124b909e8753" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256343}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f344f685-f7f7-5c43-81ea-34b1f9ab56a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-119479" :question/problem "Find the exact value of  $\\operatorname{cos}⁡{195}^{∘}.$\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that ${195}^{∘}={135}^{∘}+{60}^{∘}.$*" :question/worked-solution "Recall the sum formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\n$$\n\nApplying the sum formula for cosine with $x={135}^{∘}$ and $y={60}^{∘}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({195}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡({135}^{∘}+{60}^{∘}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡{135}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{60}^{∘}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{135}^{∘}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\  & =(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}-\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{6}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256349 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c6a58962-cb06-519a-8c64-0dfa3b9c14d7" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying Expressions in Degrees Using the Sum and Difference Formulas"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b677d3c4-e2ba-5a7f-aa4c-a85c0d6ad4b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256351} {:answer/id #uuid "3043578b-6548-5304-b79b-1ba5a0116001" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256352} {:answer/id #uuid "69dba4d0-0e08-5c54-a838-6916ad595074" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256353} {:answer/id #uuid "4802329c-97d3-58b0-92fb-16c383bc8e50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256354} {:answer/id #uuid "32da348e-790a-5334-8bdf-03d780af6158" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256355}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b677d3c4-e2ba-5a7f-aa4c-a85c0d6ad4b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256351} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c25a0c8-a926-5024-860b-b5178f35a0ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256350}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "18b12d9d-8405-5cd0-8023-0b0321a2b50c" :question/math-academy-id "q-119482" :question/problem "$\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-{30}^{∘})=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the difference formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u-v)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for cosine with $u=x$ and $v={30}^{∘},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-{30}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256356 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "831f9aa0-099e-5e0c-8a9d-c4828b629f64" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying Expressions in Radians Using the Sum and Difference Formulas"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "959e76cc-0ba4-5431-b4ed-155c26865f39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡w-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡w)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256358} {:answer/id #uuid "1ec7c404-f956-5b56-b9a5-4a5d92151879" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡w+\\operatorname{cos}⁡w)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256359} {:answer/id #uuid "3d978735-5701-51d3-88bc-88a18cd92ace" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡w-\\operatorname{cos}⁡w)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256360} {:answer/id #uuid "59b571c6-a71a-594f-9a98-9bf8344f9cff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡w-\\operatorname{cos}⁡w)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256361} {:answer/id #uuid "3f482ba8-9fe9-5bc9-9ba3-9ea9e7daa9c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡w-\\operatorname{sin}⁡w" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256362}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "59b571c6-a71a-594f-9a98-9bf8344f9cff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡w-\\operatorname{cos}⁡w)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256361} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d798f1f-a88d-58b5-a519-607f948fe6c0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256357}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "92d4f2cb-5b8a-5636-96e9-9d32e4ef6033" :question/math-academy-id "q-119485" :question/problem "$\\operatorname{cos}⁡(w-\\frac{3\\pi }{4})=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the difference formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u-v)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for cosine with $u=w$ and $v=\\frac{3\\pi }{4},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(w-\\frac{3\\pi }{4}) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡w\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})+\\operatorname{sin}⁡w\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡w\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})+\\operatorname{sin}⁡w\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡w-\\operatorname{cos}⁡w).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256363 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "283415d8-47d7-5d42-8836-0c0b0c4efc85" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Exact Values Using the Sum and Difference Formulas"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "151861be-9456-5a82-b33f-5349f34f8739" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{6}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256365} {:answer/id #uuid "7171a9de-870e-5f12-a6e1-2905c5605f2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{6}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256366} {:answer/id #uuid "8576e8e3-13c4-5db8-a00a-99de0ba14390" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{3}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256367} {:answer/id #uuid "67553b3a-a65e-5a18-b529-9c0526cd77f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{3}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256368} {:answer/id #uuid "750639f7-1b4a-5b53-99f3-84fdca45519b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1+\\sqrt{6}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256369}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "151861be-9456-5a82-b33f-5349f34f8739" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{6}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256365} :answer-field/id #uuid "87460352-017b-57ff-94f9-972d287c7a5e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256364}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "545f61c1-c114-5ca2-a4bd-862a953a500b" :question/math-academy-id "q-141360" :question/problem "Find the exact value of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{12}).$\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $-\\frac{\\pi }{12}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$*" :question/worked-solution "Recall the difference formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for cosine with $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ and $y=\\frac{\\pi }{3},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{12}) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{6}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256370 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c6a58962-cb06-519a-8c64-0dfa3b9c14d7" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying Expressions in Degrees Using the Sum and Difference Formulas"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9f1c37e-fe49-5f41-9724-0ff54b393a71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256372} {:answer/id #uuid "758104da-c2b1-5851-99a7-c770f94c774c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :ans